cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Pytrich-LLM: Hierarchical Task Network Planning with LLM-Generated Heuristics"
abstract: >-
  Code, generated heuristics, benchmarks and results of the NeurIPS 2026 paper
  "Hierarchical Task Network Planning with LLM-Generated Heuristics". The paper
  investigates whether large language models can generate effective search
  heuristics for HTN planning, extending the methodology of Corrêa, Pereira and
  Seipp (NeurIPS 2025) from classical to hierarchical planning. Using the Pytrich
  planner on seven standard total-order HTN benchmark domains, it evaluates
  heuristics generated by nine LLMs under domain-specific prompting against two
  established domain-independent heuristics in the same planner and against the
  PANDA planner. A configuration fixed in advance solves more instances than
  either domain-independent heuristic, the best generated heuristics expand fewer
  nodes than both on most instances, and the virtual best over all models is on
  par with PANDA in coverage.
